    "type": "MCQ",
    "exam": "GATE-2021: 2M",
    "body": "Consider the following ANSI C program:\n\n#include <stdio.h>\n\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\nstruct Node{\n\nint value;\n\nstruct Node *next;};\n\nint main( ){\n\nProgramming and Data Structures\n\nstruct Node *boxE, *head, *boxN; int index = 0;\n\nboxE = head = (struct Node *) malloc(size of(struct\nNode));\n\nhead → value = index;\n\nfor (index = 1; index <= 3; index++){\n\nboxN = (struct Node *) malloc(size of(struct Node));\n\nboxE → next = boxN;\n\nboxN → value = index;\n\nboxE = boxN; }\n\nfor (index = 0; index ≤ 3; index++) {\n\nprintf (\"Value at index %d is %d\\n\", index, head →\nvalue);\n\nhead = head → next;\n\nprintf (\"Value at index %d is %d\\n\", index+1, head\n→ value); } }\n\nWhich one of the statements below is correct about the program?\n\n(a) Upon execution, the program creates a linked-\nlist of five nodes.\n\n(b) Upon execution, the program goes into an\ninfinite loop.\n\n(c) It has a missing return which will be reported as\nan error by the compiler.\n\n(d) It dereferences an uninitialized pointer that may\nresult in a run-time error.",
