    "body": "Consider the following context-free grammar where\nthe set of terminals is {a, b, c, d, f}\n\nS → d a T | R f\n\nT → a S | b a T | ε\n\nR → c a T R | ε\n\nThe following is a partially-filled LL(1) parsing table\n\nWhich one of the following choices represents the correct combinations for the numbered cells in the parsing table ('blank' denotes that the corresponding cell is empty)?\n\n(a) (1) S → R f\n(b) (1) blank\n\n(2) S → R f\n\n(2) S → R f\n\n(3) T → ε\n\n(3) T → ε\n\n(4) T → ε\n\n(4) T → ε\n\n(c) (1) S → R f\n(d) (1) blank\n\n(2) blank\n\n(2) S → R f\n\n(3) blank\n\n(3) blank\n\n(4) T → ε\n\n(4) blank",
