    "num": 5,
    "type": "MCQ",
    "exam": "GATE-2014 : 2M",
    "body": "Consider the basic block given below.\n\na = b + c\n\nc = a + d\n\nd = b + c\n\ne = d − b\n\na = e + b\n\nThe minimum number of nodes and edges present in the DAG representation of the above basic block respectively are\n\n(a) 6 and 6\n(b) 8 and 10\n\n(c) 9 and 12\n(d) 4 and 4\n\n6. [MCQ] GATE-2014 : 1M]\n\nWhich one of the following is FALSE?\n\n(a) A basic block is a sequence of instructions\nwhere control enters the sequence at the beginning and exits at the end.\n\n(b) Available expression analysis can be used for\ncommon subexpression elimination.\n\n(c) Live variable analysis can be used for dead\ncode elimination.\n\n(d) x = 4 × 5 ⇒ x = 20 is an example of common\nsubexpression elimination.",
    "subject": "Compiler Design",
