    "num": 18,
    "type": "MCQ",
    "exam": "GATE-2008 : 2M",
    "body": "The P and V operations on counting semaphores, where s is a counting semaphore, are defined as follows:\n\nP(s): s = s - 1;\n\nif s < 0 then wait;\n\nV(s): s = s + 1;\n\nif s ≤ 0 then wakeup a process waiting on s;\n\nAssume that Pb, and Vb, the wait and signal operations on binary semaphores are provided. Two binary semaphores Xb and Yb are used to implement the semaphore operations P(s) and V(s) as follows:\n\nP(s): Pb (Xb);\n\ns = s - 1;\n\nif (s < 0) {\n\nVb (Xb);\n\nPb (Yb);\n\nelse Vb(Xb);\n\nV(s): Pb (Xb);\ns = s + 1;\nif (s ≤ 0) Vb(Yb);\nVb(Xb);\n\nThe initial values of Xb and Yb are respectively\n\n(a) 0 and 0\n(b) 0 and 1\n\n(c) 1 and 0\n(d) 1 and 1",
